{"repositoryId":1413121646,"availability":"available","full":"OliverSolomon/wordcraft-react","name":"wordcraft-react","description":"Adaptation of Storytold's 1:1 reproduction of Microsoft Word. Original repo: https://github.com/storytold/wordcraft. ","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":6,"forks":1,"created":"2026-10-10T11:40:58Z","updated":"2026-10-17T13:28:40Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://oliversolomon.github.io/wordcraft-react/","topics":["microsft","word","wordcraft"],"demo":"https://oliversolomon.github.io/wordcraft-react/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T18:53:45.065Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T18:53:45.065Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T18:53:45.065Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T18:53:45.065Z","stars":6,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The WordCraft word processor, an open-source look-alike of Microsoft Word, packaged as an editor you can drop into React, Next.js or any web app, the way you would use TipTap or another WYSIWYG editor.","It isn't a re-implementation. The package ships the upstream WordCraft code itself (the ribbon, the dialogs, the page layout and the document engine), compiled from Rust to WebAssembly and pinned to one upstream commit. So what your users see is a 1:1 match with WordCraft's own web and desktop apps. What this package adds is the part an embedder needs: it mounts the editor in an element you own, gives you an API for documents and commands, and lets you handle saving instead of having the browser download a file."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/OliverSolomon/wordcraft-react/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9c4fae021984adf8c9e9962519b1836bec838499433bfdbd2cd89e0043f6dc98","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T18:53:45.143Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T18:53:45.143Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The WordCraft word processor, an open-source look-alike of Mi